    "content": "There's only one question left to answer from @Coinkite, and it's this:\n\nWhy wasn't the libNgU project hosted in the official GitHub organization side by side with the firmware repo, and why did @DocHex use an alt nym to develop it instead of his main account?\n\nMind you, given the available evidence it's impossible that @DocHex tricked everyone and managed to import this library into the firmware undetected.\n\nThe changelog for version v3.2.2 of the ColdCard's firmware includes a shout-out to @switck, and even the official @COLDCARDwallet account interacted with him on Twitter.\n\nCombine this with the fact that @nvk always claims that the CC firmware is 100% developed in-house, he had to know @switck was @DocHex: he really wasn't lying when he was saying that.\n\nPS Thank you @brashratel for bringing the changelog and this interaction to my attention.",
